  abbrev_source_title = {Computational Intelligence and Image Processing in Agriculture: Applications and Innovations},
  abstract            = {This chapter examines the transformational influence of artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML) on contemporary agriculture, emphasizing the incorporation of these technologies in improving diverse agricultural methods. The introduction of modern agriculture covers the significance of technological innovations to explore several functions of AI and ML in crop management. The discussion encompasses precision agriculture, crop surveillance and analysis, remote sensing, and the application of unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) and drones for pest and disease identification, reflecting the advantages of image recognition and predictive modelling in enhancing crop yields and health. Soil and water management are examined through innovative techniques, such as the use of sensors and IoT devices for monitoring soil health, data analysis for soil health, and the widespread implementation of smart irrigation systems for optimized water usage. This chapter also covers livestock management, focusing on AI-driven health monitoring and diagnosis via wearable devices, behavioral analysis, and automated feeding systems that utilize nutritional data analysis to enhance livestock productivity and well-being. Supply chain optimization is a vital domain examined, encompassing predictive analytics for yield forecasting, inventory management, market price prediction, and AI-driven market analysis. The utilization of autonomous agricultural technology, such as self-driving tractors, harvesters, and robots for planting, weeding, and harvesting, is emphasized for their capacity to enhance efficiency and diminish labor expenses. Smart greenhouses with AI-driven temperature control systems, energy-efficient technology, and automated fertilizer delivery systems are also discussed for their contribution to optimizing plant growth conditions. © 2026 by The Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers, Inc. All rights reserved.},
