	affiliations = {Vivekanand Education Society's Institute of Technology, Department of Computer Engineering, Mumbai, India},
	abstract = {The prices of crude oil and carbon black are important aspects of economic planning as they are highly sensitive commodities that affect the activities in global markets and industries in a significant manner. This research suggests a hybrid deep learning and ensemble learning model used in nonlinear crude oil price forecasting and the resultant forecasting of N330 grade carbon black price, one of the key inputs in the rubber and polymer sectors. The framework combines deep learning models and ensemble algorithms with the aid of feature engineered technical indicators and macroeconomic variables. The feature selection was based on correlation analysis between crude oil, natural gas and carbon black, and preprocessing ensured the quality of the data. The experimental findings revealed that the LSTM AdaBoost model was more effective in weekly crude oil prediction compared to traditional methods. The GRU AdaBoost model was more effective in monthly predictions of crude oil. The GRU XGBoost model achieved superior performance for monthly carbon black prediction. The suggested hybrid method enhances predictive accuracy and offers meaningful decision support to the stakeholders in the energy markets and similar industries.  © 2026 IEEE.},
