  abstract            = {Global food security depends heavily on agriculture, yet it is still very difficult to anticipate crop yields because of a number of dynamic elements, including soil characteristics, climate trends, and market swings. Real-time data and sophisticated machine learning algorithms are frequently absent from traditional yield estimating approaches, which results in ineffective agricultural planning and production optimizing. In order to solve this, we suggest an AI- powered crop yield projection and optimization system that makes use of a variety of input variables, including soil types, weather conditions, and acreage, in addition to historical and current crop data (2020–2025). We demonstrated great prediction accuracy by using an MLP-Regressor, achieving a Mean Squared Error (MSE) of 0.0848 and an R2 score of 0.9742. CNN's potential for richer feature extraction despite its lower accuracy was demonstrated by more experimentation, which produced an MSE of 0.2208 and an R2 score of 0.5425. Our system gives current crop price predictions based on yield and acreage, forecasts future price trends over the next five years, and incorporates a Streamlit-based user interface for real-time yield forecasts in tones and kilograms. By providing films on crop growth and fertilizer recommendations using the YouTube API, it also improves agricultural decision-making by giving farmers access to useful information for raising yield and profit. © Grenze Scientific Society, 2025.},
  affiliations        = {K.S.R.M College of Engineering, Kadapa, India; Annamacharya University, Rajampet, India},
