  pages                  = {116 - 122},
  publisher              = {Association for Computing Machinery, Inc},
  abbrev_source_title    = {Proc. Int. Conf. Big Data, Inf. Comput. Netw., BDICN},
  abstract               = {Due to the commodity characteristics of agricultural products that are affected by the perturbation of climate, environment, sudden disasters and other factors, their price laws are often difficult to capture using a single predictive model. In this paper, a VMD-PSD-LSTM-based agricultural futures price prediction model is proposed with fresh eggs as the research object. In this model, the components obtained from VMD are input into a multivariate LSTM model together with the original sequences before decomposition as characteristic variables, so as to obtain the predicted values more quickly and optimize the performance of the model. Furthermore, to demonstrate the superiority of the model, this paper evaluates the evaluation indicators of the model, compares VMD-PSO-LSTM with other models based on the same data. The results show that the model outperforms other models in all aspects of the indicators combined, and shows superior performance with higher accuracy in prediction results. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).},
