  booktitle           = {2025 International Conference on Smart Computing, IoT and Machine Learning (SIML)},
  title               = {Comparative Model Study: Gold Price Prediction Using Long Short-term Memory (LSTM) Network and Graph Convolutional Network (GCN)},
  year                = {2025},
  month               = {June},
  note                = {Cited by: 2},
  pages               = {1-5},
  publisher           = {Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.},
  abbrev_source_title = {Int. Conf. Smart Comput., IoT Mach. Learn., SIML},
  abstract            = {Gold is a valuable commodity sought by traders, investors, and many people in the financial sector. However, gold prices are determined by a very complex set of factors that influence each other. In this research, two sophisticated deep learning methods are compared, Graph Convolutional Networks (GCN) and Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) networks, for predicting gold prices. GCN excels at modeling the complex interdependencies between influencing factors, whereas LSTMs are excellent at managing long-term dependencies and sequential data. As gold prices are theoretically the same worldwide, this study uses USD-denominated gold prices. Our findings contribute to the ongoing exploration of advanced predictive models within financial forecasting. It has been proven that with proper training and hyperparameters used, there is a possibility that GCN can outperform the LSTM model which is known to function well when dealing with time-series data, achieving 0.9890 R<sup>2</sup>, 14.8055 MAE, 25.1125 RMSE, and 0.00649 MAPE. However, further research and training are required to affirm the stability of the capability of the models in predicting the values of stock prices. © 2025 IEEE.},
