  abbrev_source_title    = {IEEE Int. Conf. Autom. Control Intell. Syst., I2CACIS - Conf. Proc.},
  abstract               = {Sri Lanka's coffee industry faces plenty of challenges, from grading beans to handling disease, managing resources, and dealing with unpredictable prices. Our paper introduces an AI-powered Coffee Industry Optimization System designed to help everyone involved in the process from farmers to exporters make smarter decisions. The system stands on four main pillars. First, component is an intelligent coffee bean grading and sorting tool. This uses computer vision and embedded systems on a Raspberry Pi to sort beans and catch defects as soon as they appear. Now, there's this smart farm resource planner powered by AI. It takes a close look at soil conditions, checks the latest weather, and digs into past data to decide how much fertilizer, pesticide, and labor each farm really needs. Then there's the disease detection and yield estimation part. Here, deep learning steps in to catch plant diseases early and to guess how big the harvest will be, all based on what's actually happening in the fields right now. Lastly, there's a price prediction and advisory system for exporters, which analyzes weather and market trends to forecast coffee prices and offer tailored advice. Altogether, our system gives stakeholders a practical way to adopt smart agriculture, transforming traditional coffee farming into something more sustainable and intelligent powered by AI.  © 2026 IEEE.},
