  publisher              = {Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.},
  abbrev_source_title    = {Int. Conf. Mach. Learn., Big Data Bus. Intell., MLBDBI},
  abstract               = {[Background] Accurate prediction of sales volumes for vegetable commodities relies on high-precision time series forecasting methods. However, the volatility and weak regularity of the data pose challenges to achieving high precision in time series forecasting.[Method] This study is based on the Bi-LSTM network model and introduces an improved LSTM model for predicting the sales prices of vegetable commodities, utilizing EMD decomposition and iCHOA optimization. The enhanced network incorporates the EMD decomposition algorithm, reducing the volatility and non-stationarity of the original time series. This augmentation accelerates model training and simultaneously enhances prediction accuracy.[Result] The findings demonstrate that the enhanced model outperforms its predecessor in terms of MSE, RMSE, and MAE. Moreover, compared to the original LSTM and Bi-LSTM models, the R2 values show a notable increase of 25.1% and 33.0%, respectively, indicating the substantial improvement achieved by the proposed modifications. © 2023 IEEE.},
