  abstract            = {Plant diseases and market price volatility significantly hinder agricultural productivity, food security, and economic stability for farmers. This study presents an integrated system utilizing machine learning for two core objectives: plant disease detection using the YOLOv4 algorithm and crop price prediction using linear regression. The YOLOv4 model was trained on a balanced dataset of healthy and diseased plant leaf images from the PlantVillage dataset, achieving high accuracy suitable for real-time field application. Simultaneously, historical crop price data along with environmental variables were used to train a linear regression model for forecasting market trends. The YOLOv4 model achieved 99.99% peak accuracy in disease identification, while the linear regression model demonstrated strong predictive capabilities using RMSE and R2 evaluation metrics. This integrated framework offers practical decision-support for farmers, enhances crop management, and highlights the potential of AI-based agricultural systems to promote efficiency, sustainability, and economic resilience in farming practices. © 2025 IEEE.},
