  abstract            = {This study presents an integrated smart agriculture system that combines Internet of Things (IoT) technology with machine learning to support data driven decision making for farmers in Sri Lanka. The system brings together crop recommendation, fertilizer recommendation, crop price prediction, and equipment and labour hiring within a single mobile application. Real-time soil parameters (pH, N, P, K, temperature), weather data, and market data are fused through a unified decision engine. The fertilizer recommendation module achieved approximately 92 % classification accuracy, while fertilizer amount prediction reached an R2 of 0.96. Crop price forecasting achieved R2 values up to 0.87 depending on crop type and model selection. The hiring module applies a hybrid matching strategy combining classification and semantic similarity to improve relevance and efficiency in resource allocation. A pilot study with 32 farmers showed a 16.8% profit increase and 81.4% decision accuracy, highlighting improved productivity and decision making.  © 2026 IEEE.},
