  pages                  = {1-7},
  publisher              = {Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.},
  abbrev_source_title    = {World Conf. Commun. Comput., WCONF},
  abstract               = {Gaining insight into the future and forecasting data and graph trends is one of the top concerns of stock market investors with the goal to make the best decisions and plans for the future. Although making accurate market predictions is difficult, a number of academics in this subject have tried to solve this problem by presenting a variety of concepts, approaches, and studies. High volatility, non-stationarity, and nonlinearity are some of the characteristics of financial time series data that have created challenges and compelled researchers to constantly seek for new and more precise models for analysis This study examined a number of time-series and AI-based stock market price prediction algorithms. The NSE and Bloomberg dataset are considered for evaluation. These data are initially evaluated by using a time series algorithms called ARIMA, SARIMA, BVAR and E-GACH. Then several ML approaches such as RF, RNN, FNN and GNB are employed for evaluation. Further, Hybrid algorithms are developed for stock price prediction. LSTM-GA, BST-LSTM, ABC-ANFIS-SVM and HyRNN some hybrid approaches utilized here for comparison. These comparison shows that the ARIMA, GNB and ABC-ANFIS-SVM has better results as 92.2% NPV, 89% accuracy and 0.01 of MSE than other algorithms which are used for comparison.  © 2025 IEEE.},
