  pages     = {117-122},
  abstract  = {This research work examines the possible use of AI technology in improving efficiency in the FMCG sector. The stock market is an extremely complex area of study and operates in a dynamic manner due to several influencing factors such as investor sentiment and economic statistics. Forecasting stock prices is a complicated process that is crucial for many investors, financial analysts, and even regulators. Until recently, traditional ways to forecast stock prices included the use of statistical and technical analysis tools. But all of them face a problem – their inability to detect complex dependencies and underlying structures in financial time series. Recently, deep learning has become a promising tool in stock price prediction because of its ability to model nonlinear trends and provide meaningful information on the basis of large datasets. In this paper, stock price forecasting is explored using not only market indicators but also sentiment analysis on the basis of current events. A new algorithm of forecasting is suggested that could improve the accuracy of stock market predictions. In the paper, stock price movement prediction is investigated under various market conditions during two months. Also, a comparison between various algorithms is carried out to see how efficient they are in tracking market trends and providing predictions.},
